=== PARITY (vs web LivePowerFlowWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources → bound via the shared state-holder seam (LivePowerFlowSource → LivePowerFlowModel):
    useTeslaEnergySites, useTeslaEnergyLiveStatus(siteId), useTranslation. The production app wires
    LivePowerFlowSource over the KMP EnergyStore (StateHolderModel<LoadableState<…>>); the view performs
    NO HTTP. The web's "sites[0].energy_site_id → live-status(siteId)" chaining is the source's job.
  Projection → PowerFlowBuilder.buildProjection is a 1:1 port of the web memoized nodes/arrows:
    nodes [solar(top), grid(left), home(right), battery(bottom)] with |kW| magnitudes; arrows
    solar→home (active >0.01), solar→battery (min(solar,|batt|)), battery→home (discharge), grid→home
    (import), home→grid (export), grid→battery (charge w/o solar). Source-node arrow colors. Stroke ∝
    magnitude (1..4); compact keeps the 3 largest. Verified by an EXECUTED harness (26/26) below.
  Composition → glass WidgetShell (Workflow→`point.3.connected.trianglepath.dotted` icon + "Live Power
    Flow" title + freshness chip + refresh + optional Open) · PowerFlowDiagram (Canvas-stroked arrows
    with marching-dash flow + node circles: SF Symbol in the node color, live kW value, label outside
    the ring). Recharts→none / Leaflet→none. Web SVG `<line>`/`<circle>`/`<foreignObject>` → Canvas +
    positioned SwiftUI views (crisp symbols + numericText value).
  States (all render) → loading (skeleton chrome) · no-site ("No Tesla Energy site linked") · empty
    ("No live power data") · error (Retry) · stale (chip + banner) · offline (cached + chip + banner) ·
    content. Model phase resolution keeps cached content visible behind refresh/errors (web shell
    behavior). The web's `error={null}` shell keeps cached values; the prompt-required hard-error state
    (no cache) renders a Retry affordance.
  i18n → all source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
    widget.livePowerFlow.{title,solar,grid,home,battery,noSite,noData} (+ .description from the registry)
    → ALL PRESENT in LivePowerFlowWidget.strings. Key diff used-vs-defined = 0 drift. No English literals
    in native code (every Text routes through LivePowerFlowStrings).
  a11y → the diagram is one image element with a localized label ("Energy flow diagram") + a per-node
    value summary (LivePowerFlowAccessibility.summary); every button (refresh / retry / open) has an
    accessibilityLabel; Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce Motion pauses the dash + snaps the value roll.
  Telemetry → LivePowerFlowModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"LivePowerFlowWidget") → bridges the
    shared Telemetry.track(.screenView) (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy test.
  Registry → LivePowerFlowWidget.registration: id "live-power-flow", category "energy", default 2×4,
    min 2×4, max 4×40 (+ clamp()), matching registry/energy.ts. Asserted.

